WEBVTT

00:00.080 --> 00:01.200
Now in real projects.

00:01.200 --> 00:02.920
This happens a lot as a data analyst.

00:02.960 --> 00:08.280
You're gonna, like, be introduced to a new dataset, and someone from the business is gonna ask you

00:08.280 --> 00:13.480
a question now before jumping immediately to the new data and start like answering the question, you

00:13.480 --> 00:18.720
have to calm down and take a pre-step in order to understand first the data.

00:18.720 --> 00:25.240
So that means you have to explore the content of this new dataset by doing few analyses to get yourself

00:25.240 --> 00:26.680
familiar with the data.

00:26.680 --> 00:31.320
And this activity, we call it exploratory data analysis EDA.

00:31.480 --> 00:36.480
So that means you have to start checking some basics, like how big the data sets, what the columns

00:36.480 --> 00:39.160
means, whether we have any missing values.

00:39.160 --> 00:44.840
Then you start doing some basic stuff like grouping up by time, by regions, by products, and all

00:44.840 --> 00:45.800
those activities.

00:45.800 --> 00:47.160
Maybe has nothing to do.

00:47.200 --> 00:50.920
Yet with the real business question, you are just exploring it.

00:50.920 --> 00:57.520
So as you can see, those basic activities can get you closer to the data and it can protect you from

00:57.520 --> 01:00.280
any wrong conclusions that you give as an answer.

01:00.280 --> 01:06.600
So you can close the doors, deep dive into the data, explore it, and only then start answering the

01:06.600 --> 01:09.440
business questions that is related to this data sets.

01:09.440 --> 01:14.640
And this is exactly what we mean with EDA and why you as a data analyst, you have to master it.
